  "findings": [
    "Large external tile JSON trees synchronously constructed thousands of Cesium tiles, with tasks up to 2455 ms in the initial run.",
    "Local external fragments keep source geometry and world transforms; the latest run used about 31 MB of local header blobs and reported a maximum individual construction slice of 21.3 ms. The two-millisecond budget is cooperative, not a hard deadline.",
    "The bridge search performed a horizon terrain pick every two seconds even during flight. At the requested 75 km/h that is 41.7 metres. Navigation now uses camera coordinates; the latest two runs recorded zero such picks.",
    "Preparing the shared glTF BRDF lookup before activation removed its 1532.9 ms in-flight shader-status wait observed in the preceding run.",
    "The latest run still includes first-use model-material compilation and other long tasks, up to 648 ms. This change does not establish hitch-free flight on every device or for every new material."
  ],
  "correctnessChecks": {
    "javascriptTestsPassed": 609,
    "realCesiumHeaderEquivalence": "Exact source content resource URLs, effective world matrices, bounding sphere centres/radii and refinement/error values before and after expansion",
    "headerLifecycle": "Owned-layer hooks, multi-owner disposal, cancellation, blob/version query handling, wide/deep/multiple-content trees and embedded data URIs",
    "savedSpots": "Actual Cesium browser renderer with synthetic 1000 m terrain and a real GLB tileset at 1007 m, restored spot data and both loading orders; the generic ground control rises seven metres while the production spot remains at terrain height",
    "flightBrowserRegression": "Passed with actual Cesium synthetic terrain: graphics profiles, input/focus, GPS/Angle/Acro camera and physics, reset/exit, contact checks and camera culling during rapid rolls",
    "syntheticSchedulingChecks": "Passed: 18000 bridge-source features and 10000 stable scene frames",
    "bundledRuntime": "Cesium 1.145.0: 395 file hashes and Flutter asset paths verified"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "One diagnostic run per implementation stage, not five matched repetitions or a causal FPS comparison.",
    "Changed network arrival order, scene content, travelled distance, thermal conditions and driver cache state can change timings.",
    "75 km/h is the requested speed, not continuously achieved speed: contacts, acceleration and pause-safe elapsed-time handling shorten the travelled distance.",
    "Cesium postRender intervals do not measure displayed frames or GPU presentation time; the CPU interval starts at preUpdate and excludes earlier work.",
    "The periodic bridge focus is exercised, but API3 and Overpass discovery requests were blocked by the allowlist; this is not a complete bridge-source workload measurement.",
    "No native Windows WebView2, physical Android, thermal endurance, process peak-memory or GPU-memory measurement is asserted."
  ]
